WEBVTT

00:00.970 --> 00:03.140
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:03.140 --> 00:06.370
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:06.370 --> 00:08.950
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:08.950 --> 00:12.340
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:12.340 --> 00:15.100
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:15.100 --> 00:18.540
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:18.540 --> 00:22.960
In the 31st year of Seika, a hot-blooded girl who can run really fast

00:22.960 --> 00:27.310
plunged herself into the middle of this conflict without letting her parents know.

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

02:02.700 --> 02:07.150
Situation 06

02:02.700 --> 02:07.150
The Library Force
Did Not Fire

02:11.630 --> 02:12.780
Are they down there?

02:12.780 --> 02:13.530
No!

02:13.530 --> 02:14.940
So come up!

02:20.820 --> 02:22.680
You're so fast.

02:22.680 --> 02:24.860
It's what I'm best at.

02:25.220 --> 02:26.570
Call the base.

02:26.570 --> 02:27.780
Yes, Sir.

02:31.910 --> 02:33.540
What should I tell them?

02:33.540 --> 02:35.400
Tell them that we're in dire straits.

02:35.400 --> 02:36.550
Yes, Sir.

02:37.920 --> 02:42.760
That night, Instructor Komaki and I had gone to a used book store in Yamanashi

02:42.760 --> 02:46.450
to retrieve a valuable book known as the Book of Prophecy.

02:46.450 --> 02:49.450
Please take this.

02:49.960 --> 02:53.430
Are you sure about giving up such a valuable book?

02:53.540 --> 02:56.220
I can't sell it regardless.

02:56.220 --> 03:00.180
I want it to be read by many people.

03:00.180 --> 03:04.400
Having it in the Library is the only way to achieve that.

03:04.400 --> 03:06.490
We appreciate it.

03:14.690 --> 03:17.330
Is this book that valuable?

03:17.330 --> 03:21.840
It was censored vigorously immediately after the Cleansing Act was passed.

03:21.840 --> 03:25.190
There probably aren't any copies of it left on the market.

03:25.190 --> 03:27.250
It's a Western novel, right?

03:27.250 --> 03:29.840
It's a sci-fi novel by an American writer.

03:29.840 --> 03:31.230
Sci-fi?

03:31.230 --> 03:33.900
It's about a world where books are hunted down.

03:33.900 --> 03:38.490
The protagonist's job, as a member of a group just like the Cleansing Committee, is to burn books.

03:38.490 --> 03:40.110
That's...

03:40.110 --> 03:43.290
It's almost as if it prophesied our current situation, isn't it?

03:43.290 --> 03:46.280
It was written sixty years ago, too.

03:48.620 --> 03:50.600
That's why it's called the Book of Prophecy...

03:50.600 --> 03:53.570
A French filmmaker also made it into a movie.

03:53.570 --> 03:56.920
It's been censored as well, and you can't watch it anymore.

04:02.060 --> 04:04.840
The car behind us bothers me.

04:04.840 --> 04:06.870
Let's get off at the exit before ours.

04:06.870 --> 04:07.930
Yes, Sir.

04:16.140 --> 04:18.060
Was I worrying too much?

04:18.060 --> 04:19.690
Looks like it.

04:27.150 --> 04:29.120
They were waiting for us!

04:32.680 --> 04:33.970
It's the car from earlier!

04:33.970 --> 04:34.960
Just as I thought!

04:34.960 --> 04:37.000
We'll be the decoys!

04:52.440 --> 04:53.710
I found them!

04:54.650 --> 04:56.300
There they are!

04:57.470 --> 04:58.230
Shoot!

04:58.230 --> 04:59.720
Run!

04:59.720 --> 05:00.860
This is Genda.

05:05.040 --> 05:06.000
Halt!

05:06.000 --> 05:07.450
Or we'll shoot!

05:12.510 --> 05:14.000
Instructor Komaki!

05:14.230 --> 05:15.370
I'm fine.

05:15.370 --> 05:17.020
It's just a scratch.

05:17.840 --> 05:20.340
Who fired that shot?!

05:20.410 --> 05:24.080
Urban areas are a buffer zone as determined by the agreement!

05:24.080 --> 05:27.210
Not even the Cleansing Force has the right to fire!

05:27.790 --> 05:30.760
I'll beat you up, so step forward!

05:30.760 --> 05:33.230
Kasahara-san, this is no time for this!

05:33.230 --> 05:35.180
But...

05:37.860 --> 05:39.770
Is it from Kasahara?

05:39.770 --> 05:43.030
She called us, but hung up when I answered.

05:44.020 --> 05:47.080
She hasn't picked up since then, no matter how many times I've called.

05:47.080 --> 05:48.450
Nothing from Komaki either?

05:48.450 --> 05:50.870
Nor Sakai or Harada.

05:53.550 --> 05:57.340
Considering the time, they must be near Hachiouji or Hino.

05:59.720 --> 06:00.700
Found them?

06:00.700 --> 06:01.980
No, Sir.

06:01.980 --> 06:05.460
All right, move to the meeting point a block ahead.

06:09.380 --> 06:11.740
It was really close, but we lost them.

06:12.120 --> 06:13.760
Is your leg okay?

06:13.760 --> 06:16.520
It was just a ricocheting bullet that grazed me.

06:16.520 --> 06:18.920
But it'll be tough to run now.

06:18.920 --> 06:20.270
This is terrible.

06:23.940 --> 06:26.990
That Cleansing Force member is inexcusable.

06:29.610 --> 06:31.280
What's so funny?

06:31.280 --> 06:33.000
It's nothing.

06:54.740 --> 06:55.920
Is this Kasahara?

06:55.920 --> 06:57.520
What happened?

06:57.610 --> 06:58.780
Yes.

06:58.930 --> 07:00.930
Yes, Sir.

07:00.930 --> 07:03.170
We'll wait here until the rescue team arrives.

07:03.440 --> 07:06.870
Also, Instructor Komaki is injured.

07:06.870 --> 07:09.530
No, it's not serious, but his right calf—

07:09.530 --> 07:10.590
Kasahara-san!

07:10.590 --> 07:12.530
The Cleansing Force shot at him!

07:12.530 --> 07:14.530
In a residential area, too!

07:14.530 --> 07:16.530
They're in Hino!

07:16.530 --> 07:18.260
Head there immediately with some men.

07:18.260 --> 07:19.040
Yes, Sir.

07:19.040 --> 07:20.380
Let's go!

07:20.600 --> 07:22.540
Was LOSC Komaki injured?

07:22.540 --> 07:24.540
She said he was shot in the leg.

07:24.540 --> 07:26.760
It's not a serious injury, though.

07:27.040 --> 07:28.800
Damn them!

07:29.130 --> 07:30.340
Hurry, Tezuka!

07:30.340 --> 07:31.480
Yes, Sir!

07:32.930 --> 07:34.240
Thanks.

07:34.240 --> 07:37.080
You didn't have to tell them about my injury.

07:37.080 --> 07:39.700
It'll only make them needlessly concerned.

07:39.700 --> 07:42.000
I have an obligation to report it.

07:42.000 --> 07:43.430
Also...

07:43.430 --> 07:48.110
You can't forgive the Cleansing Force member who fired a shot in a residential area?

07:48.110 --> 07:51.440
I will ask the Force to protest it firmly later.

07:51.440 --> 07:52.810
It'll be useless.

07:52.810 --> 07:57.630
They had silencers on, so nobody in the neighborhood will have noticed it so late at night.

07:57.630 --> 08:02.190
What about your wound and the ricochet mark on the cement?

08:02.190 --> 08:04.910
They'll make an excuse of some sort.

08:04.910 --> 08:10.470
In their eyes, the rules are not there to be followed, but to be broken in crafty ways.

08:11.840 --> 08:13.610
No! No! Stay away!

08:13.610 --> 08:15.260
No!

08:20.190 --> 08:22.820
Damn it, now I won't be able to go to the bathroom.

08:23.670 --> 08:27.550
I thought I'd enjoy a single's life, but...

08:37.740 --> 08:38.790
Shoot!

08:38.790 --> 08:39.920
What's the matter?

08:39.920 --> 08:42.620
The phone battery is almost dead.

08:44.230 --> 08:47.030
I guess mine got broken earlier.

08:47.030 --> 08:50.560
Well, all we need to do is wait for the rescue team.

08:51.810 --> 08:53.440
Instructor Komaki,

08:53.440 --> 08:55.890
why did you laugh earlier?

08:58.210 --> 08:59.980
Tell me!

08:59.980 --> 09:02.850
It really wasn't an appropriate time to laugh!

09:02.850 --> 09:04.940
Well...

09:11.570 --> 09:13.460
They aren't in this sector.

09:14.530 --> 09:17.740
We can't find them, even after so much searching...

09:17.740 --> 09:19.950
Where are they hiding?

09:21.330 --> 09:22.570
The Hino switchyard...

09:22.570 --> 09:23.220
What?

09:23.220 --> 09:24.450
They're in the Hino switchyard!

09:24.450 --> 09:28.290
Call the railroad company and get permission to search inside their facility!

09:28.780 --> 09:31.950
Remind them that we won't hinder their train schedules.

09:31.950 --> 09:33.840
We'll move out!

09:33.840 --> 09:34.910
Yes, Sir!

09:38.140 --> 09:40.150
Please be safe.

09:42.180 --> 09:45.830
Tell me why you laughed earlier.

09:45.830 --> 09:50.150
I was just thinking about how much you always resemble him.

09:51.030 --> 09:53.420
Your demonic instructor...

09:54.120 --> 09:56.380
It's a long story...

09:56.380 --> 09:58.580
but I guess that's okay.

09:58.580 --> 10:01.760
We have nothing to do until the rescue team gets here anyway.

10:01.760 --> 10:04.350
I know I'm the one who asked,

10:04.840 --> 10:10.930
but stories involving Instructor Dojo are often painful to me as well,

10:10.930 --> 10:13.430
so please go easy on me.

10:16.190 --> 10:19.690
During the year after Dojo and I joined the Library Force,

10:19.690 --> 10:22.600
the year before we were assigned to the Task Force,

10:22.600 --> 10:26.780
there was a battle involving the books stored at a children's center in Tokyo.

10:26.780 --> 10:28.830
The Task Force was called to action.

10:28.830 --> 10:34.140
Dojo and I hadn't joined the Task Force yet, but they expected us to do so eventually because we graduated from a library school,

10:34.140 --> 10:36.060
so they took us with them too.

10:38.940 --> 10:43.430
Their object of pride was a large collection of children's books.

10:43.430 --> 10:46.890
They had rare books not found anywhere else.

10:46.890 --> 10:48.560
The Cleansing Committee focused there and came after those books.

10:48.560 --> 10:51.240
The reason you joined the Library Force was because of a children's book, wasn't it?

10:54.940 --> 10:56.090
Yes.

10:56.090 --> 10:59.280
So children's books get targeted a lot?

10:59.280 --> 11:06.340
Children's books clearly reveal the world's absurdities that adults can no longer see.

11:06.340 --> 11:10.100
So their existence must be bad for the Committee.

11:10.100 --> 11:16.440
Our society turned out like this because of political reasons,

11:16.440 --> 11:21.660
but if people from a place with no Media Cleansing Act or Freedom of Library Act saw this,

11:21.660 --> 11:25.060
it would seem ridiculous and incomprehensible to them.

11:26.130 --> 11:27.700
True.

11:27.700 --> 11:33.220
But unfortunately, this is our reality.

11:42.540 --> 11:47.080
Man, where did all those people come from?

11:48.660 --> 11:50.280
Looks like breaking through them won't be possible.

11:50.280 --> 11:51.240
Yeah.

11:51.240 --> 11:53.690
They have far more people than we do,

11:53.690 --> 11:56.130
and we can't have a big shoot-out here.

11:56.130 --> 12:00.820
LOSC Dojo, the Cleansing Force fired at LOSC Komaki, right?

12:00.820 --> 12:03.380
That's what Kasahara seems to have said.

12:03.380 --> 12:04.340
What about it?

12:04.340 --> 12:05.820
Nothing.

12:06.530 --> 12:09.280
Let's search around and do recon with fewer guards.

12:17.700 --> 12:21.370
The battle, which started in the middle of the night, came to a stalemate.

12:21.370 --> 12:23.120
That's when morning dawned.

12:23.120 --> 12:25.580
Fire to the left!

12:28.730 --> 12:31.420
The battle will end when the facility opens.

12:31.420 --> 12:33.260
That means our victory.

12:33.260 --> 12:35.830
Don't let them enter the building until then!

12:35.830 --> 12:36.970
Roger!

12:36.970 --> 12:39.510
We couldn't break through from the right either!

12:40.170 --> 12:42.180
10 minutes to opening...

12:42.180 --> 12:45.130
It's about time to offer them a cease-fire.

12:45.130 --> 12:47.150
The children's center is closed today!

12:47.150 --> 12:48.030
Go away!

12:48.030 --> 12:49.150
Let us in!

12:49.150 --> 12:50.790
We came to feed the bunnies.

12:50.790 --> 12:51.940
No!

12:52.670 --> 12:54.210
What is he doing?

12:54.210 --> 12:57.000
He must be getting edgy because they're about to lose.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.950
These are the carrots grandma prepared!

12:58.950 --> 13:00.570
Shut up and go away!

13:01.840 --> 13:03.620
Hey! Wait!

13:07.010 --> 13:08.110
No way!

13:18.910 --> 13:20.240
He shot at him?

13:20.240 --> 13:22.800
It was only a warning shot, though.

13:24.380 --> 13:29.140
The shot landed ten meters away from the kid.

13:29.140 --> 13:30.090
But still...

13:30.090 --> 13:33.510
Yes, it was a preposterous act.

13:33.510 --> 13:35.220
It made me upset too.

13:35.220 --> 13:39.350
But I heard something really snap next to me,

13:39.350 --> 13:42.770
and Dojo was running out before I realized it or had time to stop him.

13:42.770 --> 13:44.280
Hey!

13:44.990 --> 13:46.990
Who fired that shot?

13:46.990 --> 13:50.310
I'll beat you up, so step forward!

13:53.930 --> 13:56.420
I knew that was it.

13:56.420 --> 13:59.370
I was really impressed.

13:59.370 --> 14:04.180
Is it the result of Dojo's teachings, or a natural instinct of yours?

14:04.180 --> 14:06.050
I don't like it either way!

14:11.020 --> 14:13.260
It's only a matter of time before they find us here.

14:13.260 --> 14:14.850
I'll be the decoy.

14:14.850 --> 14:17.450
Please get away from here with the Book of Prophecy.

14:17.450 --> 14:20.870
See, that's just like how Dojo used to act, too.

14:20.870 --> 14:22.670
But...

14:22.670 --> 14:26.780
What's important is to not let them have the Book of Prophecy.

14:51.210 --> 14:52.390
There they are!

14:58.640 --> 15:00.460
Kasahara-san, that's enough.

15:00.460 --> 15:03.360
There's no need to injure each other needlessly.

15:03.710 --> 15:06.650
Hey! Don't treat me so roughly!

15:10.790 --> 15:13.180
Neither of them have the Book of Prophecy.

15:13.180 --> 15:14.580
What?!

15:15.320 --> 15:16.940
Did you hide it?

15:16.940 --> 15:17.720
What?

15:17.720 --> 15:19.400
Are you going to stick a needle between my finger and fingernail?

15:19.400 --> 15:22.990
I don't think they'd do that in this day and age.

15:22.990 --> 15:27.890
I don't care about myself, but don't mistreat our female member.

15:27.890 --> 15:30.260
You'll regret your actions.

15:30.770 --> 15:36.010
I don't think you'd tell us if we interrogated you normally.

15:36.010 --> 15:39.130
We'll comb the place and find it.

15:48.280 --> 15:49.290
Anyone get hurt?

15:49.290 --> 15:51.770
We only got scratched up.

15:51.770 --> 15:54.980
They probably got two or three broken ribs.

15:54.980 --> 15:57.080
You always overdo it!

15:57.080 --> 15:59.920
I don't want to hear that from you!

16:00.130 --> 16:02.650
By the way, about the story earlier...

16:02.650 --> 16:08.480
What happened after Instructor Dojo charged out alone?

16:08.480 --> 16:10.140
That?

16:11.950 --> 16:13.810
Who fired that shot?

16:13.810 --> 16:16.270
I'll beat you up, so step forward!

16:17.060 --> 16:19.190
You scum!

16:20.010 --> 16:23.740
Dojo got beat up badly by the Cleansing Force then, but...

16:23.740 --> 16:27.070
Don't let Dojo get all the action!

16:27.070 --> 16:31.740
We were lead by LSTC Genda, so we would never just watch...

16:32.670 --> 16:36.320
We all charged in under his order,

16:36.320 --> 16:39.290
and I have no idea what really happened after that.

16:48.700 --> 16:53.340
Dojo had to make a written apology after that incident.

16:56.750 --> 17:02.870
I guess that's when the captain decided to make Dojo a squad leader, and pair him up with me.

17:03.590 --> 17:10.070
He said a brash person like Dojo needed to be in a position of responsibility, or else he'd continue to be uncontrollable.

17:20.520 --> 17:22.040
The first train, huh...

17:28.530 --> 17:30.450
Hey! Stop that train!

17:30.450 --> 17:31.200
Hurry!

17:31.200 --> 17:33.730
Excuse me, I need to go to the bathroom!

17:33.730 --> 17:35.800
I can't hold it any more!

17:35.800 --> 17:36.450
Shut up!

17:36.450 --> 17:39.470
I'll tell you where the book is if you let me go!

17:39.470 --> 17:40.350
Silence!

17:40.610 --> 17:43.080
The Book of Prophecy is on that train!

17:43.080 --> 17:45.770
Stop that train; I don't care who!

17:52.440 --> 17:54.110
The Library Force is attacking us!

17:54.110 --> 17:55.550
What?

17:55.550 --> 17:57.410
I'll go, then!

17:57.410 --> 17:59.420
Enoki, that's enough.

18:00.100 --> 18:01.800
I said that's enough.

18:01.800 --> 18:05.800
But Sir! The book is on that train!

18:05.800 --> 18:07.010
We can still make it!

18:07.010 --> 18:10.350
The Department of Justice requested the Committee to stop.

18:10.350 --> 18:12.400
The DoJ did?

18:12.400 --> 18:14.230
No way!

18:14.230 --> 18:18.430
There was a complaint filed by the residents regarding shots being fired.

18:18.660 --> 18:20.050
This mission is over.

18:20.050 --> 18:21.340
Retreat!

18:25.880 --> 18:27.310
Everyone okay?

18:27.310 --> 18:29.740
Yeah, we're fine.

18:33.860 --> 18:36.130
Who shot Komaki?

18:44.980 --> 18:46.790
Was it you?

18:52.280 --> 18:53.670
Are you going to punch him?

18:53.670 --> 18:55.790
Are you really punching him?

18:55.790 --> 18:57.640
Instructor Dojo!

19:00.570 --> 19:05.120
We will file a vehement complaint about this breach of our agreement.

19:05.120 --> 19:06.600
Don't think you can get away with this!

19:12.900 --> 19:16.700
Dojo is a madman, but he's capable of learning.

19:16.700 --> 19:18.470
You should learn from him.

19:18.470 --> 19:19.710
Yes, Sir!

19:28.460 --> 19:32.540
The call just came in to let us know that the Book of Prophecy was picked up safely at Hino Station.

19:32.540 --> 19:35.940
With that, the mission is finally complete.

19:35.940 --> 19:40.660
I'm surprised with how quickly the Cleansing Force retreated.

19:40.660 --> 19:43.840
They said that the DoJ requested them to stop.

19:43.840 --> 19:47.840
It's also hard to believe that the residents filed the complaint, too.

19:47.840 --> 19:52.030
The DoJ taking action so early in the morning isn't normal either.

19:52.210 --> 19:54.380
A complaint to the DoJ?

20:01.820 --> 20:03.420
No way...

20:18.360 --> 20:20.400
I'm home.

20:30.830 --> 20:34.980
And while I was in a life-and-death situation...

20:40.510 --> 20:42.350
20 missed calls?

20:42.350 --> 20:47.310
Shibasaki

20:54.310 --> 20:55.370
thanks.

21:06.790 --> 21:10.130
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.790 --> 21:10.130
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.130 --> 21:13.510
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.130 --> 21:13.510
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.510 --> 21:18.520
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.510 --> 21:18.520
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.180 --> 21:26.860
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.180 --> 21:26.860
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.860 --> 21:36.530
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.860 --> 21:36.530
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.980 --> 21:40.510
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.980 --> 21:40.510
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.510 --> 21:43.830
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.510 --> 21:43.830
Goodbye my old self

21:43.830 --> 21:50.360
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:43.830 --> 21:50.360
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:50.360 --> 21:54.100
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:50.360 --> 21:54.100
